baseline: dependency_up{postgres}=1, outbox_oldest_pending_age_seconds=0, alerts={'PostgresReplicaLag': 'firing', 'BackupMissing': 'pending'}

## scenario 1: kill outbox publisher, then one camera ENTRY → outbox row stays PENDING
camera event → HTTP 200 (t=0.0s)
OutboxLag pending after 31.6s (age>30s threshold), age=30.937637s
OutboxLag FIRING after 43.8s total (expected ≈ 30s threshold + 12s for + ≤6s scrape/refresh)

## scenario 2: stop PostgreSQL (pg_ctl stop -m fast)
PostgresPrimaryDown pending after 4.0s, dependency_up{postgres}=0, offline_mode_active=0
PostgresPrimaryDown FIRING after 10.0s (expected ≈ 6s for + ≤6s detection)
camera event during outage → HTTP 202 (202 = offline buffer)
PostgreSQL back → PostgresPrimaryDown resolved after 3.5s, dependency_up{postgres}=1

final alerts: {'PostgresReplicaLag': 'firing', 'BackupMissing': 'pending', 'OutboxLag': 'firing'}

